deploy_gate:
  instruction: Before deploying MiniModel.org, make sure MiniModel.org documentation, catalogs, workspace.uai, and public-safe talisman exports reflect the current source state and the TinyRustLM integration behavior.
  requirements:
    - Keep the metadata-only catalog boundary explicit; project servers do not run or serve user model bytes.
    - Update related docs on TinyRustLM.com, TinyRustLM.MiRust.com, MiniModel.org, MiRust.com, and any remaining retired-site redirect/public-export surfaces when source options, manifests, verifier behavior, or legal/liability language changes.
    - Run relevant pointer audits and git diff --check before packaging or deployment.
required_private_read_order:
  - workspace.uai
  - .uai/index.uai
  - .uai/totem.uai
  - .uai/taboo.uai
  - .uai/talisman.uai
  - .uai/file-handoff.uai
  - .uai/intake-outcome-ledger.uai
  - .uai/short-term-memory.uai
current_state:
  - MiniModel.org is the Rust-first P2P tiny model package exchange roadmap site.
  - Source options are user-owned local files/lists, user-triggered Hugging Face discovery, local Hugging Face conversion-request/script handoff, local share metadata export after verified `.slm` import, one-command `prepare-peer-share` sender packaging, manifest+peer-offer catalog-entry writing, late `add-peer-source` consenting peer metadata publication, portable `write-peer-source-announcement` metadata, `write-peer-source-announcement-feed` metadata publication, same-origin checksum-bound peer-source announcement feed routes via `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcement-feed`, maintainer-side `apply-peer-source-announcements` drift checks, batch `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcements` publication, metadata-only `write-catalog-snapshot` reuse, optional catalog-listed consenting peer sources, direct known-peer HTTP piece serve/fetch, one-command TinyRustLM peer-import request execution, and future broader P2P discovery/relay; all converge on local `.slm` verification.
  - First implementation code now includes a Rust verifier workspace: `crates/minimodel-core` plus `crates/minimodel`, line-oriented manifest parsing, `serde_json` parsing for TinyRustLM peer-import request JSON and catalog snapshot validation, real q8 fixture manifest, local `.slm` artifact verification, chunk/Merkle checks, one-command `prepare-peer-share` output from a local `.slm` into MiniModel manifest plus `.minimodel-peer-offer` plus local peer pieces plus catalog entry, drift-checked `write-catalog-entry` output from manifest plus `.minimodel-peer-offer`, `add-peer-source` output that validates a proof-ready entry and attaches one consenting direct peer URL, `write-peer-source-announcement` output that binds model id/artifact checksum/peer-offer proof/catalog-entry checksum to one consenting peer URL, `apply-peer-source-announcements` output that rejects drift and deduplicates peer URLs before catalog publication, `write-peer-source-announcement-feed` output that validates portable announcements into a metadata-only feed, `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcement-feed` output that binds a same-origin feed route into `models.v0.json` by SHA-256, batch `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcements` output that validates entries plus announcements and rejects unmatched announcement model ids, metadata-only `write-catalog-snapshot` output after duplicate/model-byte/peer-source rejection, optional `peer_source_count`/`peer_sources` metadata after known-peer URL validation, local peer-piece export, direct HTTP peer-piece serving/fetch with project-server host rejection, peer-piece reassembly, `import-peer-request` receiver execution, and basename-only import receipts.
  - The July 2 TinyRustLM/MiniModel intake synthesis is routed as a durable constraint: Hugging Face rows are metadata only until local Rust conversion or P2P import, proof-ready rows are not called runnable, and converted-once availability is published through peer-source metadata without project servers hosting bytes.
  - The live public-safe export is verified.
  - Direct public .uai and agent-file-handoff access is denied.
